      "text": "To find the minimum possible value of the sum\n\n\\[\nS = \\frac{a}{2b} + \\frac{b}{4c} + \\frac{c}{8a},\n\\]\n\nwe can use the AM-GM (Arithmetic Mean - Geometric Mean) inequality. The AM-GM inequality states that for any non-negative real numbers \\(x, y, z\\),\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x + y + z}{3} \\geq \\sqrt[3]{xyz},\n\\]\n\nwith equality if and only if \\(x = y = z\\).\n\nLet's consider the expression \\( S = \\frac{a}{2b} + \\frac{b}{4c} + \\frac{c}{8a} \\). To apply AM-GM, we will first rewrite \\(S\\) in a form that allows us to directly use the inequality:\n\n\\[\nS = \\frac{a}{2b} + \\frac{b}{4c} + \\frac{c}{8a}.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find a way to apply AM-GM to this sum. Notice that:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{2b} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a}{b},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{b}{4c} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{c}{8a} = \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot \\frac{c}{a}.\n\\]\n\nNow, let's consider the arithmetic mean of these terms. Let:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a}{b}, \\quad y = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c}, \\quad z = \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot \\frac{c}{a}.\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\n\\[\nx + y + z = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c} + \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot \\frac{c}{a}.\n\\]\n\nWe need to show that:\n\n\\[\nx + y + z \\geq 3 \\sqrt[3]{\\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a}{b} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c} \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot \\frac{c}{a} \\right)}.\n\\]\n\nCalculating the product inside the cube root, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a}{b} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c} \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot \\frac{c}{a} \\right) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{1}{32}.\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{32}} = \\frac{1}{3}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\nx + y + z \\geq 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = 1.\n\\]\n\nEquality in AM-GM holds when \\(x = y = z\\). So we set:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c} = \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot \\frac{c}{a}.\n\\]\n\nFrom \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c}\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{b}{c},\n\\]\n\nwhich implies \\(\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{b}{c}\\). Hence, \\(a: b = b: c\\). Let \\(a = kb\\) and \\(b = kc\\) for some constant \\(k\\). Then:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{c}{a} = \\frac{c}{kb} = \\frac{1}{k} \\cdot kc = c.\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{c}{8a} = \\frac{c}{8kb} = \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot kb = \\frac{a}{8k}.\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\nx + y + z = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c} + \\frac{c}{8a} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{b}{c} \\right) + \\frac{c}{8a}.\n\\]\n\nFrom \\(\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{b}{c}\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{b}{c} = 2.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\nx + y + z = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 + \\frac{c}{8a} = 1 + \\frac{c}{8a}.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(x = y = z\\), we have:\n\n\\[\nx + y + z = 1 + \\frac{c}{8a} \\geq 1 + 1 = 2.\n\\]\n\nHence, the minimum possible value of \\(S\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}.\n\\]",
